; CommonTree3 — Forest terrain variant: a third ROUND-CANOPY broadleaf, matching CommonTree1
; and CommonTree2 exactly in texture set, bark and leaf language.
;
; THIS SLOT USED TO BE A CONIFER, AND THE CONIFER IS NOT COMING BACK FROM THIS KIT. A narrow
; tapered pine was added on 2026-08-16 to answer "every tree looks the same", removed later as
; the project's only Poly Pizza asset, restored as MegaKit Pine1 during the standardisation, and
; then removed AGAIN on 2026-09-08 after a human look at all five variants side by side. The
; reason is in the assets, not in taste:
;
;   - Pine1 renders as a SOLID CONE. Its foliage is `Leaf_Pine_C.png`, a single flat frond
;     silhouette, over only 770 canopy triangles — against CommonTree1's 1920 of individually
;     cut leaves. It reads as a different KIND of asset beside its siblings, not a different
;     species.
;   - ALL FIVE pines in the kit (Pine_1..5) use that same frond texture. Pine_4 and Pine_5 carry
;     more canopy geometry (1210 / 1158 tris) and would break up more, but none of them has
;     CommonTree's leaf-cutout look. There is no pine here that matches.
;   - The tall layered conifers in the pack's own Preview_4.jpg are NOT in this download.
;     `Leaves_GiantPine_C.png` ships in Textures/, but no GiantPine mesh exists in glTF, FBX or
;     OBJ — the free Standard set is 68 of 116 models and the giant pines are among the 48 that
;     are not included. The preview advertises the PRO kit.
;
; So the conifer silhouette is UNAVAILABLE from the standardised pack, not merely unchosen.
; Re-adding one means either buying the PRO kit or accepting a second pack in Forest, which is
; the exact thing the standardisation removed. Do not re-add Pine1 as a look fix.
;
; SCALE: raw mesh AABB height 9.42519 -> scaled 0.26525 for the ~2.5 tile-unit canopy every
; Forest tree targets (CommonTree1's shipped 0.344 x 7.264786 = 2.499). Height stays a control
; variable across the terrain; only silhouette and foliage differ.
;
; 1800 canopy triangles — nearly CommonTree1's 1920 — so it carries the same leaf density and
; will not read as the "cheap" one of the three.
;
; SHORTENED TO 1.9 TILE-UNITS (2026-09-08, human ruling: "lower the common tree 3, by even
; more"). Scale 0.26525 -> 0.20159 against a raw mesh AABB height of 9.42519
; (0.20159 x 9.42519 = 1.900).
;
; THE THREE BROADLEAF TREES NOW FORM A DELIBERATE HEIGHT LADDER, and this is the shortest rung:
;   CommonTree1  2.5 tile-units  "Tree - Tall"
;   CommonTree2  2.2             "Tree - Medium"
;   CommonTree3  1.9             "Tree - Short"
; Even 0.3-unit steps. This REPLACES the older "height is a control variable, only silhouette
; differs" rule that the other Forest headers state — with three near-identical round-canopy
; meshes, height IS the variety, and an even canopy line was the thing that read as monotonous.
; TwistedTree1 and BushCommon are outside the ladder: the first is a different silhouette
; entirely, the second is undergrowth at the ~0.6 shrub class.
;
; If a fourth broadleaf is ever added, extend the ladder rather than parking it at 2.5 — three
; graded heights and one more at the top would undo the effect.
[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3]

